# CodFlow server — local development secrets
# Copy this file to .dev.vars and fill in your values.
# (.dev.vars is gitignored — your real values never get committed.)

# ── Required for local dev ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Used by the storefront (cod-astro) and dashboard to authenticate against the
# server's store API. Generate one with:  openssl rand -hex 32
# It is hashed with SHA-256 before storage (see scripts/seed-local.mjs).
# STORE_API_KEY=

# Better Auth signing secret — the SAME value must be set on cod-client-astro
# (both workers share the auth D1 tables). Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
# BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=

# ── Only needed if you exercise the R2 image presign flow locally ─────────────
# (R2 credentials are stored as wrangler secrets in production:
#  `wrangler secret put CF_ACCOUNT_ID` etc. — do not put them in wrangler.toml.)

# Your Cloudflare account ID — the long hex string on your Cloudflare dashboard.
# CF_ACCOUNT_ID=
# R2 API token access key id (https://dash.cloudflare.com/profile/api-tokens → R2)
# R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# R2 API token secret access key
# R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=

# ── Optional overrides ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Overrides the [vars] block in wrangler.toml for local runs if you need to test
# MCP token verification against a live dashboard, or a different environment:
# ENVIRONMENT=development
# BETTER_AUTH_URL=http://localhost:4321/api/auth
# WORKER_SELF_URL=http://localhost:8787/
# WORKER_URL=http://localhost:8787
# MEDIA_DOMAIN=media.example.com
# R2_BUCKET_NAME=codflow-images

# ── MCP SDK v2 (used by the stateless elicitation + OAuth work) ───────────────
# HMAC key that seals stateless MCP elicitation request state (must be >= 32
# bytes). Generate one with:  openssl rand -hex 32
# MCP_REQUEST_STATE_KEY=

# HMAC key shared with the Astro dashboard for MCP OAuth login tickets
# (must be >= 32 bytes). Set the SAME value on cod-client-astro. Generate with:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
# MCP_LOGIN_TICKET_SECRET=

# Cookie-encryption key for the @cloudflare/workers-oauth-provider consent flow.
# Generate one with:  openssl rand -hex 32
# COOKIE_ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# In production all values are set with `wrangler secret put`, never in code.
